From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 20:59:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] util: make the event signaller and waiter explicit

Event assumed eventfd semantics: one object doing both jobs, with try_clone
handing out another. Nothing said which end was meant to signal and which to
wait, so the answer lived in the order the callers happened to clone in.

Replace it with create_event_pair(), returning an EventSignaler that only
signals and an EventWaiter that only waits. The fence paths then read the way
they work: the end that waits keeps the waiter and the other half goes to the
peer.

This also gives platforms where the two ends are genuinely different rights
somewhere to put them. An eventfd is symmetric and does not care.
---
 src/virtio/magma-gpu-rs/lib/util/mod.rs       |  4 +-
 .../magma-gpu-rs/lib/util/sys/linux/event.rs  | 93 +++++++++++++++----
 .../magma-gpu-rs/lib/util/sys/stub/event.rs   | 54 ++++++++---
 .../lib/util/sys/windows/event.rs             | 54 ++++++++---
 .../virtgpu_kumquat/virtgpu_kumquat_impl.rs   | 36 ++++---
 5 files changed, 189 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

